WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:14.430
The first-ever edition of the Daily Mirror
came with a free mirror.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.340
No one has ever seen an atom.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:23.760
They're too small to be seen by a microscope
and can't be counted or weighed individually.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:29.910
For 48 years after tinned food was invented,
people who wanted to eat it had to use a hammer

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:31.320
and chisel.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.070
The can opener wasn't invented until 1858.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:40.440
People in Victorian Britain who couldn't afford
chimney sweeps dropped live geese down their

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.370
chimneys instead.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:49.420
Pigeons can tell the difference between impressionist
paintings by Monet and cubist works by Picasso.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.930
They can even tell when the Monets are hung
upside down.

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:59.219
Tour de France riders need to eat the equivalent
of 27 cheeseburgers a day.

00:00:59.219 --> 00:01:06.850
Summer on Neptune lasts for 40 years, but
the temperature is minus 200°C.

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:11.590
The name of the first human being in Norse
mythology was Ask.

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:19.280
The technology behind most smartphones relies
on up to 250,000 separate patents.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:26.390
On a clear, moonless night the human eye can
detect a match being struck 50 miles away.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:34.259
The International Space Station is as roomy
as a five-bedroom house and travels at 17,500

00:01:34.259 --> 00:01:35.259
mph.

00:01:35.259 --> 00:01:41.009
The Bank of America was originally called
the Bank of Italy.

00:01:41.009 --> 00:01:48.120
Lightning strikes the Earth 8.6 million times
a day or about 100 times a second.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:53.110
The screwdriver was invented a hundred years
before the screw.

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:56.549
It was originally used to extract nails.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:02:03.149
The tadpoles of the South American paradoxical
frog are larger than the frog itself.

00:02:03.149 --> 00:02:10.349
The whole works of Shakespeare contains only
about 20,000 different words – less than

00:02:10.349 --> 00:02:18.200
half the vocabulary of the average English
speaker today.

